# bench/json-compare/main.ts run on sample.json: `<workload> <iterations> <at>:`
# and the checksum line it prints. Every comparator (simdjson, yyjson,
# RapidJSON, serde_json, Go) that has the workload printed the same line for
# the same arguments when this was recorded, the f64 sum spelt each language's
# way; tests/run.js holds the Nish program to it without a network. `at` is
# the offset run.mjs's rules pick: for tokenize the last digit that follows a
# digit, for typed the last digit of the first performance's `start`.
# typed-reuse is Nish's alone, and must print typed's line.
tokenize 7 1361: tokenize 6981962826702482149 161 7.000092727189358e+22 3672931878305861320
typed 7 957: typed 645623151590338983 2
typed-reuse 7 957: typed 645623151590338983 2
serialize 7 -1: serialize 11183316248078939317 741
